  "notes": [
    "059: existing Foundry-generated pixel still reused; no new image or video API call.",
    "Landmarks authored against 1817x805 source; head RIGHT. Source SL uses caudal base x265 to snout x1805; not total image width.",
    "Body thickness is an artistic conditional assumption, not measured species width.",
    "Profile approval means operator landmark calibration only; model visual review remains pending.",
    "059c: side eyes moved to two independent native pixel surface patches; painted body eyes replaced with same-source cheek donor. Tip UV donor suppresses ring-shaped single-side mouth projection; simplified closed snout, no jaw rig.",
    "059d: Foundry-generated, reviewed frontal auxiliary head image; eye pigment excluded from frontal projection so two side eye patches remain sole eye owners. Mouth stays static.",
    "059f: pectoral length proxy 059e=17.66% authored SL, below published20.3–26.2%; geometry extended1.32 about same root with original pixel donor remap. Revised target20.0–26.5%SL frozen before this revision; permits root landmark uncertainty.",
    "059g user-requested snout refinement: replace rapid knife-like taper after source x1680 with fuller rounded sections. End half-width0.008->0.022 native units; wider upper/lower jaw envelope. No biological mouth-width measurement claimed. Eye center, all fin definitions, spine and motion parameters retained.",
    "059h: preserve059g mesh, replace normal-switched head patches with one continuous derived head atlas. Side open-jaw pigment removed to avoid double lips. Source files unchanged; atlas colors are a declared derivation.",
    "059j: restore original upward mouth slit. Rounded nose raised progressively8–45 source pixels afterx1680; mouth-corner UV lowered beforex1600. Continuous atlas retained; offsets also applied to anterior cap. Source pixels unchanged.",
    "060a: real static oral cleft, roof/floor and lip bevel; lower jaw tip projects beyond upper. Production dimensions are hypotheses informed by species description and museum adult specimen; no jaw articulation claimed.",
    "061a: 060b rejected by user as simian. Rebuild anterior sections as converging jaw wedge, anterior height100px->20px; shorten and lift lower-jaw bottom, remove upper muzzle bulb. Thin end is a production hypothesis from qualitative same-species museum photo, not a measured width. Static mouth and no anatomical acceptance.",
    "061b: 061a converged but looked overly pinched; retain33px terminal height and broaden tip laterally. Neither width nor exact closed bite is biologically measured.",
    "061c: museum head comparison reveals prior eye centered only~30sourcepx below local roof despite44px radius. Shift eye center40sourcepx ventral; original eye donor/radius retained, surface patch reprojected. This is a qualitative landmark correction, not exact specimen morphometrics.",
    "062a: user correction: slit too long; terminal lip edge should turn down, lower lip protrudes and visibly overlaps. Shorten corner1605->1665; curved slit apex1782/452 then tip1805/468; add actual local skin lip roll, stronger lower lip. Only anterior lower envelope adjusted to house thick roll; no whole-chin inflation. Exact tissue fold is a production interpretation pending visual review.",
    "062c: dense cap lattice and cross-section lip inflation before manifold boolean; omit secondary edge bevel which produced microscopic wedges. Original body resolution increased to160x96 for smoother lip surface."
  ],
